From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 00:29:06 +0200
Subject: usb: phy: generic: Only request the vbus regulator when it is wired

The vbus regulator is requested with devm_regulator_get_exclusive(),
which the regulator core refuses to satisfy with a dummy regulator, so
the nop transceivers auto-created by MUSB glue code (which carry no
of_node or properties at all) warn on every probe:

  usb_phy_generic usb_phy_generic.3.auto: dummy supplies not allowed
  for exclusive requests (id=vbus)

Request the regulator only when a vbus-supply is actually described.
No in-tree platform provides "vbus" for this device via regulator
lookup tables.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/usb/phy/phy-generic.c | 14 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/phy/phy-generic.c b/drivers/usb/phy/phy-generic.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/phy/phy-generic.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/phy/phy-generic.c
@@ -238,12 +238,14 @@ int usb_phy_gen_create_phy(struct device *dev, struct usb_phy_generic *nop)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(nop->vcc),
 				     "could not get vcc regulator\n");
 
-	nop->vbus_draw = devm_regulator_get_exclusive(dev, "vbus");
-	if (PTR_ERR(nop->vbus_draw) == -ENODEV)
-		nop->vbus_draw = NULL;
-	if (IS_ERR(nop->vbus_draw))
-		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(nop->vbus_draw),
-				     "could not get vbus regulator\n");
+	if (device_property_present(dev, "vbus-supply")) {
+		nop->vbus_draw = devm_regulator_get_exclusive(dev, "vbus");
+		if (PTR_ERR(nop->vbus_draw) == -ENODEV)
+			nop->vbus_draw = NULL;
+		if (IS_ERR(nop->vbus_draw))
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(nop->vbus_draw),
+					     "could not get vbus regulator\n");
+	}
 
 	nop->dev		= dev;
 	nop->phy.dev		= nop->dev;
-- 
